# Deeds (AutonomousPlayerDeeds): a bot of the player's realm who WITNESSED something the real player did tells the
# realm in /faction a few minutes later ("deed"), and other bots react right after ("deed_reply"). Second-hand topics
# (rep_*) are a bot who did not see it, repeating the player's reputation. Every topic gets {player}, {player_class}
# (lower case), {place} (zone), and {nickname} ("the Slayer") only if the player has one: a line with {nickname} is
# skipped when there is none. The player is a real person, so the roasts tease and never wound. Real swear words are
# not in the corpus (build_corpus.py BANNED); they swear the way 2003 chat did. New writing.

